4. Added mocks both in the wrapper and the main component for redundancy
5. Simplified the provider structure
6. Used Object.assign for cleaner mock assignment
7. Ensured all required data is available before first render
8. Removed unnecessary state management
9. Provided all required hook data directly

This simplified approach should work better because:
1. It avoids context timing issues
2. Provides hooks data before the component renders
3. Reduces complexity by removing context providers
4. Ensures consistent data across all hooks
5. Mocks are in place before any hook calls

The component should now have access to all the data it needs without relying on context providers. This approach is more direct and should resolve the context-related errors.

